#
# The defect classes this distribution DECLARES (mtools:W670, W999), planted one at a time by the
# `:mutants` runner: <module>|<name>|<pattern>|<replacement>|<scope>. Each is a mistake a plausible
# edit could make that `body -> raise` cannot express (the def is still called, only its verdict
# moves). A line that stops matching is a STALE declaration and fails the grid as UNAPPLIED.
# A pattern cannot hold a literal pipe: use \S.
#
# suite_pragmas, tree_root and import_edges. corpus.py and suite_discovery.py are not declared yet.

# suite_pragmas.py: a suite declares its own deps and tenant; an absent or unreadable declaration is
# the empty answer, and a tenant outside the caller's admitted set declares nothing.
src/mikemol/corpus/suite_pragmas.py|unreadable-suite-raises|except OSError:|except KeyError:|def=_source
src/mikemol/corpus/suite_pragmas.py|whole-pragma-line-returned|match\.group\(1\)|match.group(0)|def=_captured
src/mikemol/corpus/suite_pragmas.py|requirements-not-trimmed|tuple\(p\.strip\(\) for p in declared\.split\(","\) if p\.strip\(\)\)|tuple(declared.split(","))|def=requires
src/mikemol/corpus/suite_pragmas.py|empty-requirement-kept| if p\.strip\(\)\)|)|def=requires
src/mikemol/corpus/suite_pragmas.py|unadmitted-tenant-invented|declared is not None and declared in admitted|declared is not None|def=tenant
src/mikemol/corpus/suite_pragmas.py|tenant-flag-without-dashes|f"--\{declared\}"|declared|def=tenant

